</script>

# Card

Groups related content on a bordered surface, or renders an anchor when given an `href`. Compose it from `Card`, `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardAction`, `CardContent`, and `CardFooter`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardContent, CardFooter } from "#lib/components/ui/card/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<Card>
	<CardHeader>
		<CardTitle>Notifications</CardTitle>
		<CardDescription>Choose what you hear about.</CardDescription>
	</CardHeader>
	<CardContent>
		<p>You have 3 unread messages.</p>
	</CardContent>
	<CardFooter>
		<Button size="sm">Mark as read</Button>
		<Button size="sm" variant="ghost">Settings</Button>
	</CardFooter>
</Card>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/card.json
```

## Action

Place `CardAction` inside `CardHeader` to show trailing content, such as an icon, badge, or button. It sits in a second column beside the title and description.

<Demo section="action" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Card>
	<CardHeader>
		<CardTitle>Team members</CardTitle>
		<CardDescription>Invite people to your project.</CardDescription>
		<CardAction>
			<Button size="sm" variant="outline">Invite</Button>
		</CardAction>
	</CardHeader>
</Card>
```

## Links

Pass `href` to render an anchor that highlights on hover. A disabled link drops its `href`, sets `aria-disabled`, and leaves the tab order. Without `href`, `disabled` only dims the card.

<Demo section="links" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardAction } from "#lib/components/ui/card/index.js";
	import { ChevronRightIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Card href="/docs/components">
	<CardHeader>
		<CardTitle>Browse components</CardTitle>
		<CardDescription>Opens the components list.</CardDescription>
		<CardAction><ChevronRightIcon /></CardAction>
	</CardHeader>
</Card>
```

## Size

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the padding, gap, and radius. It defaults to `lg`, with 24 pixel padding and the extra large 14 pixel radius, like the shadcn card. `xs` also shrinks the text.

<Demo section="size" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Card size="sm">
	<CardHeader>
		<CardTitle>Size sm</CardTitle>
		<CardDescription>Tighter padding and gap.</CardDescription>
	</CardHeader>
</Card>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius, which follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Card rounded="3xl">
	<CardHeader>
		<CardTitle>Rounded 3xl</CardTitle>
	</CardHeader>
</Card>
```

## Login form

Compose a card with `Label`, `Input`, and `Button` to build a login form. The submit button sits in `CardFooter`, outside the `form`, so it points at the form with the `form` attribute.

<Demo section="login" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardAction, CardContent, CardFooter } from "#lib/components/ui/card/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
	import { Input } from "#lib/components/ui/input/index.js";
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";
</script>

<Card class="login">
	<CardHeader>
		<CardTitle>Login to your account</CardTitle>
		<CardDescription>Enter your email below to login to your account</CardDescription>
		<CardAction>
			<Button variant="link">Sign Up</Button>
		</CardAction>
	</CardHeader>
	<CardContent>
		<form id="loginForm" class="loginForm">
			<div class="loginField">
				<Label for="email">Email</Label>
				<Input id="email" type="email" placeholder="m@example.com" required />
			</div>
			<div class="loginField">
				<div class="loginLabelRow">
					<Label for="password">Password</Label>
					<a href="##">Forgot your password?</a>
				</div>
				<Input id="password" type="password" required />
			</div>
		</form>
	</CardContent>
	<CardFooter class="loginFooter">
		<Button type="submit" form="loginForm" class="loginButton">Login</Button>
		<Button variant="outline" class="loginButton">Login with Google</Button>
	</CardFooter>
</Card>

<style>
	:global(.login) {
		max-width: 24rem;
	}

	.loginForm {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--spacing-xl);
	}

	.loginField {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--spacing-sm);
	}

	.loginLabelRow {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	:global(.loginFooter) {
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	:global(.loginButton) {
		width: 100%;
	}
</style>
```

## API

The `Card` props extend the native `div` attributes, or the `a` attributes when `href` is set. `CardHeader` and `CardFooter` extend the `header` and `footer` attributes, `CardDescription` extends `p`, and the other parts extend `div`. Extra attributes and event handlers such as `onclick` pass through to each element.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface CardBaseProps {
	/** Padding, gap, and radius on the shared scale; defaults to `lg` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
	/** Dims the card; a disabled link also drops its href and leaves the tab order */
	disabled?: boolean;
}
```
